{"name":"Cheek Red","hex":"#a55a55","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cheek","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The soft skin on each side of the face, below the eyes; the outer surface of the sides of the oral cavity.","The lower part of the buttocks that is often exposed beneath very brief underwear, swimwear, or extremely short shorts."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be impudent towards.","To pull a horse's head back toward the saddle using the cheek strap of the bridle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheek"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cheek","blocks":[{"text":"The cheeks constitute the area of the face below the eyes and between the nose and the left or right ear. Buccal means relating to the cheek. In humans, the region is innervated by the buccal nerve. The area between the inside of the cheek and the teeth and gums is called the vestibule or buccal pouch or buccal cavity and forms part of the mouth. In other animals, the cheeks may also be referred to as \"jowls\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Cheek.jpg/330px-Cheek.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheek","wikidata":"Q47038"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Sobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png/500px-Sobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Sobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png/1280px-Sobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Sobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png/500px-Sobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASobo_1909_260_-_Zygomaticus_major_muscle.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Chipmunk_with_Full_Cheeks.jpg/500px-Chipmunk_with_Full_Cheeks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Chipmunk_with_Full_Cheeks.jpg/1280px-Chipmunk_with_Full_Cheeks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Chipmunk_with_Full_Cheeks.jpg/500px-Chipmunk_with_Full_Cheeks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pars